    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0451" n="363" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg363"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3355: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gibson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-13T16:00:00-03:00">October 13, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 13—3:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. Minister of Foreign Affairs tells me he has conferred at length on the Chaco
                    question with President Justo<anchor n="41" xml:id="d327-f1"/> who has thus far
                    been considered an obstacle to solution. Justo expressed himself much gratified
                    and authorized his Foreign Minister to sign with Mello Franco yesterday a
                    hastily drafted “secret agreement” as to the terms of a fresh proposal to be
                    made to Paraguay and Bolivia. He said this would not conflict with the effort of
                    the League of Nations but would be “parallel to it”.</p>
                <p>The press has published the text of the joint telegram sent by the Presidents of
                    Argentina and Brazil to the Presidents of Bolivia and Paraguay exhorting them to
                    submit the Chaco conflict to arbitration—also replies which express desire of
                    both countries to find a peaceful solution but which in no way commit
                        them.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d327-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d327-f1" n="41" xml:id="d327-f1-content">
                <p>President of Argentina.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d327-f2" n="42" xml:id="d327-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence, see Republica de Bolivia, Ministerio de Relaciones Exteriores
                    y Culto, <hi rendition="#italic">Memoria presentada al Congreso de 1934.
                        Conflicto del Chaco</hi> (La Paz, Editorial “Renacimiento”, 1934), pp.
                    443–446; Republica del Paraguay, Ministerio de Relaciones Exteriores, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Libro Blanco, III Parte, Documentos Relativos al Mandato
                        de la Liga de Las Naciones a los Gobiernos del ABCP</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Proposition del 25 de Agosto de 1933</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">y al Acta del 11 de Octubre de 1933</hi> (Asunción,
                    Imprenta Nacional, 1934), pp. 71–85.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
